.claude/

# ad-hoc production data dumps left in the repo root. control.txt is 1295
# rows of `<uuid>|<md5>` and one `git add -A` from being in history forever.
control.txt
*.dump.txt

# database backups — belt and braces only. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC, and a pg_dump
# is 664 tenants' CNICs, phone numbers and full financial history. A .gitignore
# entry is not a security control: `git add -f` overrides it, and anything
# committed to a public repo is permanently public even after a force-push.
# Real backups therefore live OUTSIDE the working tree (~/HMS-backups), and
# these patterns exist only to catch a stray file, never to make one safe.
*.dump
*.dump.gpg
*.sql.gz
*.backup
backups/
